whether you use it or not we all know  about siri the voice assistant that  comes along with all iphones despite the  almost universal familiarity with siri  not many people know about series  founders a common misconception is that  steve jobs created siri or that it was  created by the apple team but this is  not the case siri was founded by three  men named dan cutlass tom gruber and  adam share  and in april of 2010 apple paid 200  million dollars to acquire siri and  spearhead themselves into the voice  assistance space  so here's what happened to series  founders and where they are today  starting off with tom gruber tom is an  american computer scientist who was born  in 1959  i would say that tom was the brainiac of  the group as he was extremely  well-educated for his bachelor's tom  attended loyola university in new  orleans where he got a double major in  psychology and computer science he  graduated sama kumari in 1981 which is  the highest latin honors indicating that  he was part of the top five percent of  his graduating class after completing  his bachelor's tom turned around and  attended the university of massachusetts  amherst where he majored in computer and  information science tom was actually  working on something similar to siri way  back in the 1980s for his master's  research tom developed a communication  assistant for individuals with severe  physical disabilities anyway tom  graduated with his masters in 1994 and  tom would find himself at the university  of massachusetts amherst once again for  his phd his doctoral paper was called  the acquisition of strategic knowledge  and it was about how computer assistance  could acquire strategic knowledge from  experts as you can see tom was on this  computer assistant slash aipath from  very early on but he still had a very  long way to go before siri after he got  his phd in 1988 dom became a research  associate at the knowledge systems  laboratory at stanford for six years  the three main research projects he  worked on at stanford include how things  work shade and knowledge sharing  technology at this point tom was 35  years old and he had spent basically his  entire life in academia in 1994 he  decided to finally change this by  getting a job at enterprise integration  technologies as senior project leader  that same year tom created a free  program called hyper mail that helped  users create email archives kevin hughes  revised and rewrote tom's code before  the release and hypermail is actually  still used to this day by most email  clients on unix and linux in 1995 tom  left his project leader job and created  his own company called introspect  software the company specializes in  helping commercial customers with  collaborative knowledge management given  how niche of a market they targeted the  company never blew up into the billions  or anything but it does seem like  they're still around and employed  between 50 and 100 people tom didn't  join syria up until january of 2008 when  the company completed its first private  funding round the initial goal of the  project was to create a conversational  medium that gave users access to all the  information in the world despite its  ambitious goal siri was more or less  just a backburner project throughout the  1990s and early 2000s one of the other  co-founders adam chair says that it  wasn't until the launch of the iphone  that they really knew where to take siri  in the few years following the launch of  the iphone the trio worked on turning  the research project into an app and in  february of 2010 siri was launched as an  app on the apple app store at the time  the trio was planning to expand the app  to android and blackberry when they  randomly got a call from steve jobs just  two weeks after the launch steve invited  a three to his house where he made his  acquisition intentions clear while the  trio was extremely happy to meet with  steve and felt that their efforts were  finally validated the trio didn't have  any plans of actually selling the app so  they would decline steve's offer but  steve didn't take no for an answer he  kept in touch with the trio over the  next few months and eventually convinced  them that he was the guy who could take  siri to the next level steve promised  that siri wouldn't just be a tiny  feature but rather an integral part of  many apple devices i think steve was  being sincere with this promise as siri  did become a major part of apple but  unfortunately it wasn't exactly how the  founders envisioned it the problem was  that apple placed a major emphasis on  search as opposed to improving series  conversational abilities as the founders  wanted this was one of the main reasons  that google and amazon were able to  quickly make up ground and arguably  overtake apple within the voice  assistance space despite this rather  bittersweet result tom stuck around at  apple for quite a bit of time tom served  as the head of series advanced  development group up until july 2018  at that point he was nearly 60 years old  and had made plenty of money from siri  so he basically just retired and has  been focusing on photography and ocean  conservation he has been involved in a  couple of tech projects since his  departure but it looks like his favorite  endeavor is a non-profit called  humanistic ai the company focuses on  encouraging collaboration between humans  and artificial intelligence as opposed  to replacing humans with ai  but that's pretty much it for tom gruber  moving on to adam cher we have the  father of siri adam was born in 1966 or  1967 presumably in sharon massachusetts  where he attended sharon high school  after graduating from high school in  1994 adam attended brandeis university  where he majored in computer science  following his bachelor's adam scored a  job as a computer scientist at sri  international's artificial intelligence  center adam would return to university  just a couple of years later though and  earn a master's in computer science and  artificial intelligence from ucla in  1993.  after getting his masters adam returned  to sri international and got to work on  the first prototype of siri  adam says that as soon as he started  working with computers in the early  1990s he knew that figuring out ways to  interact with machines in a more natural  way was the future  over the next several years adam ended  up creating dozens of siri prototypes  but the biggest catalyst for siri didn't  come until 2003. in 2003 darpa gave sri  international funding to build a virtual  assistant darpa was hoping that this  virtual assistant could be used by  military commanders and though that  never quite panned out darpa's funding  did allow sri to employ 500 engineers to  work on siri for five years after  funding from darpa started to dry up in  2008 adam secured 8.5 million from  private investors and this is when dan  and tom would get involved this  investment allowed them to create the  siri app and sell their company to steve  jobs at the same time adam also started  working on some other startups in 2007  he co-founded change.org which is an  extremely popular petitioning website  with over 400 million users that same  year adam also co-founded sentient  technologies which is more of a  background ai company one of their most  notable works includes collaborating  with mit to create an ai-powered blood  pressure tool that could predict the  likelihood of sepsis in icu patients  anyway jumping forward to after the  acquisition adam was made the director  of engineering at apple  adam didn't stick around for very long  after steve jobs death though  disappointed in the direction of siri  adam left apple in september of 2012 and  it created a new virtual assistant  startup with siri's other founder dan  given their history with siri it wasn't  too difficult to get a crap ton of money  from investors and get their startup  vive labs off the ground  in contrast to siri we focused on  creating an open platform assistant that  could support external plugins and guess  what in october of 2016 adam and dan  would sell bblabs none other than  samsung for 215 million dollars  samsung would eventually implement this  technology into their bixby virtual  assistant so not only did adam and dan  sell a company to apple but they also  sold the company to samsung truly quite  impressive and ironic at the same time  adam stuck around at samsung for a  decent amount of time but he left  samsung as well in july of 2020. since  then adam has taken on a bunch of  advisor roles at a variety of companies  including riva health auto.ai halt labs  evolve technologies brilliant labs and  the brandeis university science advisory  council but that's pretty much it for  adam and that brings us to siri's last  co-founder dan kittles  unfortunately dan is the least known of  the three founders and there's very  little information about him online  but this doesn't mean that dan wasn't an  integral part of siri dan is a norwegian  entrepreneur who spent most of his  childhood in norway it wasn't until  college that dan came to america  dan attended indiana university  bloomington where he majored in  economics after he graduated in 1999  though dan returned to norway where he  worked as a barista at an upscale pub  called lectern dan did eventually pursue  an nba but this time he decided to stay  in norway opting to attend bi norwegian  business school after graduation dan  eventually found himself working at the  telenor mobile norway's national  telecommunications business as the vice  president he stayed there until 2002  when he jumped over to motorola as  general manager for about five years  after motorola dan became an  entrepreneur in residence at the  stanford research institute in june of  2007  this is where he would get introduced  adam and tom and the rest is history fun  fact dan was actually the one that came  up with the name siri which translates  to beautiful woman who will lead you to  victory norwegian  anyway after the acquisition dan was the  first to openly express his discontent  in the direction of siri he said quote  i'm not happy with where it is today  considering the lead we had when we  launched it they should be way ahead by  now  i don't think you'd be surprised to hear  that dan was the first to leave apple in  october of 2011 right after steve job's  death at first dan was planning on  simply retiring and writing a novel  but after adam quit apple as well the  duo would end up founding vive labs the  following september  after samsung acquired beef labs dan  became a vice president at samsung but  once again he was the first leave  samsung as well in june of 2019  this time dan did take a little over a  year off but soon enough he would  co-found another company called riba  health in november of 2020. riva health  is looking to allow users to measure  their blood pressure in a clinically  approved way using smartphones it's  still in the very early stages so we'll  have to see how it goes but dan believes  that riva health could be a key step in  identifying and preventing heart disease  early on  and that's what happened to series  founders which virtual assistant do you  think is the best comment that down  below  also drop a like if you think series  founders are underrated and of course  consider joining our discord community  to suggest future video ideas and  consider subscribing to see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm ari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  [Music]  you
 

